Source: maluos-branding
Section: misc
Priority: important
Maintainer: Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/maludb/maluos
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: maluos-branding
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: MaluOS identity: os-release, issue, motd, GRUB, apt
 /usr/lib/os-release is a symlink to the variant's file (server, or
 desktop with maluos-desktop-branding), the base-files copy is diverted
 so upgrades keep working. ID=maluos, ID_LIKE="ubuntu debian": tools that
 know Ubuntu recognise a derivative; NAME, PRETTY_NAME and the URLs say
 MaluOS. Also writes /etc/issue, issue.net, lsb-release and legal, the
 MaluOS motd, GRUB_DISTRIBUTOR, unattended-upgrades origins, and turns
 off Ubuntu's Pro and motd-news advertising.

Package: maluos-desktop-branding
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, maluos-branding (>= 0.3.0)
Description: MaluOS identity for the desktop: login screen, wallpaper, session name
 Switches os-release to VARIANT="Desktop", puts the MaluOS logo and
 wallpaper on the login screen and the desktop (gsettings overrides),
 ships the MaluOS wallpapers and the distributor icon shown by Settings,
 and names the session MaluOS on the login screen.
